Let $\vec{k} = [k]_1^N$. If $\exists i < j < N$, with $k_i \geq 1, k_j \leq 1$, then $F_N^{\vec{k}} = 0$.  egin{proof} 
oindent Assume first $k_j = 0$. Using lemma ef{F_cond_lemma} we get $$ F_N^{\vec{k}} \equiv \left.  rac{\partial^{\omega(\vec{k})} F_N(\vec{\epsilon})}{\partial \epsilon_1^{k_1},..,\partial \epsilon_N^{k_N}} ight|_{\vec{\epsilon} = 0} = \left.  rac{\partial^{\omega(\vec{k})} F_{N-j+1}([\epsilon]_j^N)}{\partial \epsilon_1^{k_1},..,\partial \epsilon_N^{k_N}} ight|_{\vec{\epsilon} = 0} = $$  egin{equation}  rac{\partial^{\omega(\vec{k})-1}}{\partial \epsilon_1^{k_1},.., \partial \epsilon_i^{k_i-1},.., \partial \epsilon_N^{k_N}} \left[\left.  rac{\partial F_{N-j+1}([\epsilon]_j^N)}{\partial \epsilon_i} ight] ight|_{\vec{\epsilon} = 0} = 0 \end{equation} 
oindent Assume now $k_j = 1$. Write the probability of $Z$: $$ P([Z]_1^N) = \sum_{[X]_1^N} P([X]_1^N) P([Z]_1^N | [X]_1^N) = $$  egin{equation} \sum_{[X]_1^N} P([X]_1^N) \prod_{i=1}^N (\delta_{X_i Z_i} + \epsilon_i t_{X_i Z_i})\end{equation} 
oindent where $\delta$ is Kronecker's delta. Differentiate with respect to $\epsilon_j$: $$ \left.  rac{\partial P([Z]_1^N)}{\partial \epsilon_j} ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} = $$ $$ \left. \sum_{[X]_1^N} \left[ P([X]_1^N) t_{X_j Z_j} \prod_{i 
eq j} (\delta_{X_i Z_i} + \epsilon_i t_{X_i Z_i}) ight] ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} = $$  egin{equation} \left. \left\{ \sum_{r=1}^{s} t_{X_i r} P({[Z]_1^N}^{(j 	o r)}) ight\} ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} \end{equation} 
oindent Using Bayes' rule $P(Z_N | [Z]_1^{N-1}) =  rac{P([Z]_1^N)}{P([Z]_1^{N-1})}$, we get: $$ \left.  rac{\partial P(Z_N | [Z]_1^{N-1})}{\partial \epsilon_j} ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} = $$ $$  rac{1}{P([Z]_1^{N-1})} \sum_{r=1}^{s} t_{X_i r} \left[ P({[Z]_1^N}^{(j 	o r)}) - ight. $$  egin{equation} \left. \left. P(Z_N | [Z]_1^{N-1} ) P({[Z]_1^{N-1}}^{(j 	o r)}) ight] ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} \end{equation} 
oindent This gives: $$ \left.  rac{\partial [P([Z]_1^N) \log P(Z_N | [Z]_1^{N-1})]}{\partial \epsilon_j} ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} = $$ $$ \sum_{r=1}^{s} t_{X_i r} \left\{ P({[Z]_1^N}^{(j 	o r)}) \log P(Z_N | [Z]_1^{N-1}) + ight. $$  egin{equation} \left. \left. P({[Z]_1^N}^{(j 	o r)}) - P(Z_N | [Z]_1^{N-1}) P({[Z]_1^{N-1}}^{(j 	o r)})ight\} ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} \end{equation} 
oindent And therefore: $$ \left.  rac{\partial F_N}{\partial \epsilon_j} ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} = $$ $$ -\sum_{r=1}^{s} t_{X_i r} \Biggl\{ \sum_{[Z]_1^N} \left[ P({[Z]_1^N}^{(j 	o r)}) \log P(Z_N | [Z]_1^{N-1}) - ight. $$ $$ \left. \left. P(Z_N | [Z]_1^{N-1}) P({[Z]_1^{N-1}}^{(j 	o r)}) ight] \Biggr\} ight|_{\epsilon_j = 0} = $$ $$ \Biggl\{ -\sum_{r=1}^{s} t_{X_i r} \sum_{[Z]_j^N} \left[ P({[Z]_j^N}^{(1 	o r)}) \log P(Z_N | [Z]_j^{N-1}) - ight. $$  egin{equation} \left. \left. P(Z_N | [Z]_j^{N-1}) P({[Z]_j^{N-1}}^{(1 	o r)}) ight] \Biggr\} ight|_{\epsilon_1 = 0} \end{equation} 
